docs/prd.md

# Generated indexer output stays out of git: nodes.jsonl / edges.jsonl are a
# pure function of the working tree, so committing them buys nothing a re-index
# cannot rebuild while making every branch that touches code conflict (see
# docs/migrations/2026-08-06-stop-committing-derived-graph.md). Applies at any
# depth (the root repo federates indexer/ and mcp/ as nested repos).
# Everything AUTHORED is the exception: nothing can regenerate rationale or
# prose, so it is un-ignored below.
**/.reposkein/*
!**/.reposkein/decisions/
# ...but never half-written temp files a crashed writer left behind.
**/.reposkein/decisions/.*
# Authored summaries are committed too (per ADR 2026-08-07: derived stays
# out, authored goes in). Sharded into summaries/<xx>.jsonl since 2026-08-20 so
# two branches summarising different code never write the same file; the
# pre-sharding single file stays un-ignored while repos migrate off it.
!**/.reposkein/summaries/
**/.reposkein/summaries/.*
!**/.reposkein/summaries.jsonl
# The config RepoSkein itself runs on: repo identity, settings, and the rules
# that keep the derived graph out of git. Small, rarely edited, and needed by
# every clone — including our own, which is the point of dogfooding them.
!**/.reposkein/meta.json
!**/.reposkein/config.toml
!**/.reposkein/.gitignore
!**/.reposkein/.gitattributes

# Local-only working docs (plans, skill scratch) — never commit.
docs/superpowers/

# Cached indexer binary (postinstall fetch, M4-D1) — never commit.
mcp/bin/

# Local agent/session artifacts — never commit.
.claude/
.omo/

# Python bytecode (embed-server runs locally during dev).
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Per-machine MCP config written by setup: absolute paths + a local backend
# password. Regenerated by `reposkein-mcp init`; only .reposkein/ is shared.
.mcp.json
opencode.json

# Dependency dirs (mcp/ has its own; a stray npx/vitest run can create one at root).
node_modules/
